details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two ceramic bowls centered on an aged oak table, with one bowl sharp in the foreground and the second softly blurred in the background. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, ensuring every component is visible with generous negative space around the bowls. Soft, natural side light from a window to the left creates gentle shadows and highlights the creamy texture of the dressing. The dish consists of golden-brown, pan-seared tofu cubes resting beside tender, vibrant green asparagus pieces and a hearty base of fluffy cooked quinoa. The bowl is packed with bright red halved cherry tomatoes and plump chickpeas, all tossed with dried oregano and aromatic garlic powder. A generous swirl of pale, creamy tahini-yogurt dressing is drizzled over the top, with small drips clinging to the side of the ceramic bowl. Props include a rumpled linen napkin tucked beside the bowl and a few scattered herb leaves and a small piece of squeezed lemon on the wood surface. The textures are authentic: crispy tofu edges, softened tomato skins, and matte quinoa grains. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures a warm, lived-in kitchen atmosphere, reflecting a meal just finished. Include slight imperfections like uneven tofu browning, a small sauce drip on the rim, and a stray crumb trail. Warm, golden-hour lighting. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry, no hands, no text, no logos. The image is indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
]
